; A stressed vowel's rise. Four cards a frame in: u, its segment's kind and s, and the pitch so far; per frame the
; pitch out. In a vowel with stress 1 (or 2) the pitch rises by r0 = 15 (or 7) percent of it at the vowel's start,
; falling off to 40 percent of that at its end: + r0 - r0 6 u / 100. r0 is b f / 100 by Horner over f's two digits;
; each product is a jump into the row of nine ADD y (90-98), which runs into 99 and back.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   u        03-19: a frame: is it a stressed vowel's
  04                    INP   kind
  05                    INP   s
  06                    INP   b
  07                    CLA   kind
  08                    SUB   n2
  09                    TAC   v
  10                    JMP   out
  11            v       CLA   s
  12                    SUB   00
  13                    TAC   out
  14                    SUB   00
  15                    TAC   r15
  16                    CLA   c7
  17                    JMP   rr
  18            r15     CLA   c15
  19            rr      STO   f
  20                    CLA   b        20-41: r0 = b f / 100
  21                    STO   y
  22                    CLA   f
  23                    SFT   33
  24                    STO   d
  25                    CLA   cj
  26                    SUB   d
  27                    STO   j1
  28                    CLA   z
  29            j1      DATA  0        (JMP 99-c)
  30                    SFT   01
  31                    STO   t
  32                    CLA   f
  33                    SFT   23
  34                    STO   d
  35                    CLA   cj
  36                    SUB   d
  37                    STO   j2
  38                    CLA   t
  39            j2      DATA  0        (JMP 99-b)
  40                    SFT   01
  41                    STO   r0
  42                    STO   y        42-61: r0 u, then 6 times that, / 100
  43                    CLA   cj
  44                    SUB   u
  45                    STO   j3
  46                    CLA   z
  47            j3      DATA  0        (JMP 99-u)
  48                    STO   y
  49                    CLA   cj
  50                    SUB   six
  51                    STO   j4
  52                    CLA   z
  53            j4      DATA  0        (JMP 93)
  54                    SFT   02
  55                    STO   t
  56                    CLA   b
  57                    ADD   r0
  58                    SUB   t
  59                    STO   b
  60            out     OUT   b
  61                    JMP   frm
  70            kind    DATA  0
  71            s       DATA  0
  73            u       DATA  0
  74            b       DATA  0
  75            f       DATA  0
  76            y       DATA  0
  77            d       DATA  0
  78            t       DATA  0
  79            r0      DATA  0
  80            z       DATA  0
  81            n2      DATA  2
  82            c7      DATA  7
  83            c15     DATA  15
  84            six     DATA  6
  85            cj      JMP   99
  90            row     ADD   y        90-98: the row of nine ADD y, into 99
